body:
I think it's safe to change ActionExecutionFunction.java line 247:

```
    } catch (PackageRootResolutionException rre) {
      throw new ActionExecutionFunctionException(
          new ActionExecutionException("Failed to get cached inputs", rre, action, true));
    }
```

to

```
    } catch (PackageRootResolutionException rre) {
      actionCacheInputs = ImmutableList.of();
    }
```

For a complete fix, we should also signal back to ActionExecutionFunction.checkCacheAndExecuteIfNeeded that it should not attempt to do a cache lookup. I'm also a bit concerned about the double interpretation of ContinuationState.token == null as both cache miss and no cache lookup happened yet. Ideally, we'd represent cache misses and no lookup happened yet with different values, which would make it possible to disable the cache lookup in checkCacheAndExecuteIfNeeded by setting the token to a value indicating a cache miss.
